Section 2.13 – Displaying the Current Time

2.13.1 How do you obtain the current second, minute, and hour?

Answer:

Java provides the "Calendar" class to obtain the current hour, minute, and second.

Java Code:

import java.util.Calendar;

public class CurrentTime {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Calendar calendar = Calendar.getInstance();

        int hour = calendar.get(Calendar.HOUR_OF_DAY);
        int minute = calendar.get(Calendar.MINUTE);
        int second = calendar.get(Calendar.SECOND);

        System.out.println("Current time: "
                + hour + ":" + minute + ":" + second);
    }
}

This displays the current local time in hours, minutes, and seconds.

